Copyright © 2026 Davide Briani. All rights reserved.

1. Ownership. Everything relating to the software in this repository («tora-plugins») belongs exclusively to Davide Briani: its conception and concept, design and architecture, specifications, prototypes, source and compiled code, user interfaces and visual design, documentation, tests, scripts, configurations, development, deployment and operating procedures, know-how and every related work of authorship, invention or information, in every present and future version. Davide Briani is its author and holds all intellectual and industrial property rights, economic and moral, to the fullest extent permitted by law.

2. No licence. No licence is granted, expressly or by implication. Without Davide Briani's prior written consent it is forbidden to use, copy, reproduce, modify, translate, adapt, decompile, distribute, publish, sublicense, sell or otherwise exploit the software or any part of it, to create derivative works, and to use it to train or evaluate artificial-intelligence systems.

3. GitHub organisation and access. The repository being in the GitHub organisation «TNASRLSB», held by Davide Briani, and any access granted to collaborators or companies, including TORA NO AI S.R.L. Società Benefit, do not transfer or license any right. Any permission to use results only from a written instrument signed by Davide Briani and is revocable unless otherwise agreed in writing.

4. Third-party components. Third-party libraries, fonts and other components included or referenced remain subject to their own licences.

5. Contributions by Giacomo Sebastiani. Excluded from this attribution are the contributions of Giacomo Sebastiani (GitHub account «giacomosebastiani»): the code and documentation of which he is the author in this repository's history remain his, within the limits of the law, until assigned in writing to Davide Briani. The conception, design, specifications and every contribution other than Giacomo Sebastiani's remain Davide Briani's.

6. Governing law. This statement is governed by Italian law.
